\ fit-multinomial-ridge / predict-multinomial on the UCI Adult data.
\ Adult's income target is binary, so the multi-class target here is the
\ `relationship` column (6 levels: Husband/Not-in-family/Other-relative/
\ Own-child/Unmarried/Wife), predicted from age, education-num, hours-per-week,
\ income, and one-hot sex. The wide one-hot design would separate under the
\ plain MLE, so ridge (lambda 1) keeps the fit finite. Native-only (LAPACK via
\ lib/statistics.telic); a 2000-row prefix keeps it deterministic and quick.
"lib/statistics.telic" load
"data/adult.tsv" read-tsv 2000 iota select-rows to adult

\ relationship -> integer labels 0..K-1 by sorted-distinct position
adult :relationship @ column>array to rel
rel array>set [: :] map to classes
rel [: cell | classes cell eq where 0 @e :] map vector to y
classes size to K

\ design: numeric columns + income (already 0/1) + one-hot sex + intercept
{ } to design
design adult :age @            :age       ! drop
design adult :education-num @  :education ! drop
design adult :hours-per-week @ :hours     ! drop
design adult :income @         :income    ! drop
design adult :sex @ :sex indicators! drop
design design keys dataset>matrix with-intercept to X

X y 0 200 1e-6 1.0 fit-multinomial-ridge to beta
beta X 0 predict-multinomial to probs

\ mean probability the model assigns to each row's true class
K iota [: k | probs k @j  y k eq  * :] map 0 [: + :] reduce mean to mean-true-prob

\ === checks (stable: counts and thresholds, not the raw fitted floats) ===
"6 relationship levels detected"    [: K 6 expect= :] test
"every softmax row sums to 1"       [: probs row-sums 1 - dup * sum 1e-8 < expect :] test
"beats the 1/K uniform baseline"    [: mean-true-prob 1 K / > expect :] test
"beats the base-rate model"         [: mean-true-prob 0.3 > expect :] test
test-report
